surname>Dewitte</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Nougarede</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Van Onckelen</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Precociously germinating somatic embryos of <italic>Vitis vinifera</italic> have lower ABA and IAA levels than their germinating zygotic counterparts</article-title><source>Physiologia Plantarum</source><year>1998</year><volume>102</volume><fpage>591</fpage><lpage>595</lpage></element-citation></ref><ref id="bib23"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Finch-Savage</surname><given-names>WE</given-names></name><name><surname>Leubner-Metzger</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Seed dormancy and the control of germination</article-title><source>New Phytologist</source><year>2006</year><volume>171</volume><fpage>501</fpage><lpage>523</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16866955</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="bib24"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Flemion</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>After-ripening at 5&#x000b0;C favors germination of grape seeds</article-title><source>Contributions from the Boyce Thompson Institute</source><year>1937</year><volume>9</volume><fpage>7</fpage><lpage>15</lpage></element-citation></ref><ref id="bib25"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gan</surname><given-names>YY</given-names></name><name><surname>Li</surname><given-names>SH</given-names></name><name><surname>Song</surname><given-names>SQ</given-names></name><name><surname>Wang</surname><given-names>WQ</given-names></name><name><surname>Cheng</surname><given-names>HY</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Seed dormancy and release of grapes from different provenances</